# Subsets II – LeetCode 90

**Problem:** Generate all unique subsets of an array containing duplicate elements.

**Approach: Sorting + Recursion + Backtracking**

### Intuition

Instead of generating duplicate subsets and removing them using a set, we skip duplicate elements during recursion itself.

### Algorithm

1. Sort the original array.
2. Start recursion with index `0`.
3. Add the current subset to `ans`.
4. Run a for loop from `start` to `n-1`.
5. Skip duplicates using:
   `if(i > start && nums[i] == nums[i-1]) continue;`
6. Include the current element and make a recursive call.
7. Backtrack by removing the last element.

### Code

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    vector<vector<int>> ans;

    vector<vector<int>> subsetsWithDup(vector<int>& nums) {
        sort(nums.begin(), nums.end());

        vector<int> s;
        helper(nums, 0, s);

        return ans;
    }

    void helper(vector<int>& nums, int start, vector<int>& s) {
        ans.push_back(s);

        for(int i = start; i < nums.size(); i++) {

            if(i > start && nums[i] == nums[i-1])
                continue;

            s.push_back(nums[i]);

            helper(nums, i + 1, s);

            s.pop_back();
        }
    }
};
```

### Complexity Analysis

* **Time Complexity:** O(n × 2ⁿ) upper bound.
* **Space Complexity:** O(n × 2ⁿ) for storing subsets, excluding recursion stack.
* Recursion stack: O(n).

### Why is this better than brute force?

| Brute Force                   | Optimized                         |
| ----------------------------- | --------------------------------- |
| Generates all subsets         | Generates only unique subsets     |
| Sorts every subset            | Sorts original array once         |
| Uses set to remove duplicates | Skips duplicates during recursion |
| Extra set storage             | No set required                   |

### Important Concept

```cpp
if(i > start && nums[i] == nums[i-1])
    continue;
```

* `i > start` ensures we skip duplicates only at the same recursion level.
* `nums[i] == nums[i-1]` checks whether the current element is a duplicate of the previous one.

**Key Learning:** Avoid generating duplicate possibilities instead of generating everything and eliminating duplicates afterwards.
